{"id": "EUVD-2026-48621", "enisaUuid": "fe6eef02-53d9-3f9d-8712-4f8795dcd535", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (lm90) Add lock protection to lm90_alert\n\nSashiko reports:\n\nlm90_alert() executes in the smbus alert context and calls\nlm90_update_confreg() to disable the hardware alert line, without\nacquiring hwmon_lock.\n\nConcurrently, sysfs write operations (such as lm90_write_convrate) hold\nthe hwmon_lock, temporarily modify data->config, and then restore it.\n\nIf an alert interrupt occurs concurrently with a sysfs write, the sysfs\npath will overwrite the alert handler's modifications to data->config\nand the hardware register.\n\nThis unintentionally re-enables the hardware alert line while the alarm is\nstill active, causing an interrupt storm.\n\nAdd the missing lock to lm90_alert() to solve the problem.", "datePublished": "2026-07-24T15:23:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02b88fa993582b4fe228b4143b330b0bb9f28353", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/165ef777ec6f634a5e4b8d9b0dadca8ef91fa90e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bed1fc32e0eb653806fa98afcf55f9a311fc4ce2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0b66aae8a94c3663d47e4000b0e81b89ce32186", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/873e919e3101063a7a75989510ccfc125a4391cf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64213", "GHSA-mf77-wwf7-m2ff"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14383ae5-70f5-3f90-a4b7-2f1e8e209634", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "255028aa-516c-349a-8c48-807b1e1e88d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7a1d220ccb0cc2b808eb176fb05bf55a38179f3f <165ef777ec6f634a5e4b8d9b0dadca8ef91fa90e"}, {"id": "2a356060-d2cc-32d6-886d-dd264513172d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7a1d220ccb0cc2b808eb176fb05bf55a38179f3f <b0b66aae8a94c3663d47e4000b0e81b89ce32186"}, {"id": "30faf990-b277-3221-86ef-337df21d5532", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7a1d220ccb0cc2b808eb176fb05bf55a38179f3f <02b88fa993582b4fe228b4143b330b0bb9f28353"}, {"id": "3b48abaf-657a-3208-a104-af0efcfc3328", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.34"}, {"id": "75e4f594-199b-3cf0-ada6-26be47002ec9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "9ab17cbf-6954-3bca-92d0-e48c35fb78d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "acbbc009-ab6a-3e31-8c3c-2d3e4eed1b84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7a1d220ccb0cc2b808eb176fb05bf55a38179f3f <873e919e3101063a7a75989510ccfc125a4391cf"}, {"id": "c711e587-14bb-360c-8cb7-c0b041751fe0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "d09c3f10-f6f5-3a16-8cae-ea605278455b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "e0520c34-b0b2-3058-97e4-fb07dcb7bb09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7a1d220ccb0cc2b808eb176fb05bf55a38179f3f <bed1fc32e0eb653806fa98afcf55f9a311fc4ce2"}, {"id": "ecf21894-2a08-3ca8-90ce-b077ea9e1ffd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "98f2f6dc-82b9-31c1-9104-f8e3b267db34", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}